# Trivy scanner ignore list for Panakoes.
#
# Format: one rule id (or CVE id) per line. Optional `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` field
# sets a re-evaluation deadline (Trivy ignores the entry past that date so the
# finding resurfaces and we revisit). Path-scoped ignores are written as
# `<rule>:<path>` on one line.
#
# Each entry below MUST have a comment explaining (1) why this is a false
# positive or accepted risk, and (2) when we revisit.

# stripe-secret-token: services/billing/src/panakoes_billing/config.py
# Reason: the literal `sk_test_placeholder_replace_in_env` is a default
# placeholder for `Settings.stripe_api_key`, validated at startup to require
# an `sk_test_` prefix (TEST mode only; live keys raise at boot per the
# `_reject_live_key` validator). The string is not a real Stripe credential;
# it is dev-friendly default for local boot. Trivy's stripe-secret-token
# regex matches anything starting with `sk_test_` or `sk_live_`, which
# unavoidably catches our deliberate TEST-mode placeholder.
# Revisit: when billing config moves entirely to AWS Secrets Manager and
# the placeholder default is removed (tracked: SCOPE.md billing hardening).
# exp:2026-08-09
stripe-secret-token:services/billing/src/panakoes_billing/config.py
